Architecture Description

User Layer
Users access the blog application through an Application Load Balancer (ALB),
which distributes incoming requests to the backend web server.

Compute Layer
The application runs on an Amazon EC2 instance inside a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC).
An Amazon EBS volume provides persistent storage for the operating system and application files.

Networking Layer
A custom Amazon VPC contains Public and Private Subnets. 
Security Groups control inbound and outbound traffic to protect AWS resources.

Storage Layer
Amazon S3 stores static assets such as blog images and website content with versioning and encryption enabled.

Database Layer
Amazon RDS (MySQL) stores blog posts, user information, and application data, providing managed database services with automated backups.

Serverless Layer
When new images are uploaded to Amazon S3, an AWS Lambda function is triggered automatically.
Background tasks are handled using Amazon SQS, while Amazon SNS sends notifications for important application events.

Monitoring & Security
Amazon CloudWatch collects metrics, monitors EC2 performance, and triggers alarms based on defined thresholds.
Security is enforced through IAM, Security Groups, and AWS KMS for encryption.

Infrastructure as Code
The cloud infrastructure is provisioned using AWS CloudFormation, while AWS CLI is used for deployment and management.
